# Every layer whose own two measurements imply demand that could have gone unserved, beside
# whether anybody can say what happened to it. One row per exposed layer, in exactly one of three
# standings.
#
# The question is asked of the row
#   The three buffers are substitutes, so the question is asked of the row and never of one
#   column. An excess above the nameplate can be absorbed by running hot, by drawing on stock, or
#   by making the demand wait. A layer whose capacity buffer is empty has one route closed, which
#   is not the same fact as having nowhere to go.
#
#     a buffer nobody sized          Suspended. One route is unmeasured, so the ceiling is
#                                    unknown and no conclusion about it is available. An
#                                    excess the filer says was absorbed by running hot is
#                                    not contradicted by an empty stock room.
#     a buffer with room in it       The exposure had somewhere to go. Nothing is owed.
#     every buffer sized and empty   Every route accounted for, none with room. The demand
#                                    above the nameplate had nowhere to go, so somebody
#                                    went without and somebody has to be named.
#
# Only the third licenses a rule
#   Saying so is the whole point of classifying the other two rather than filtering them away. A
#   suspended layer and a satisfied layer are the same row to a `WHERE`, and they are opposite
#   facts: one says the filing is fine, the other says nobody looked.
#   algebra/exposure_standing.sqlc holds the three to a partition so a layer cannot fall out of
#   all of them and quietly shrink the population.
#
# The arm order is the precedence
#   It is deliberate. Ignorance outranks room: a layer with stock to spare and an unmeasured queue
#   is suspended, because the spare stock does not tell you whether the queue held anything.
-- layers/remainder.sqlc where exposure > 0, classified by layers/absorption.sqlc.
SELECT r.*, a.absorbable, a.unknown,
       CASE WHEN a.unknown    > 0 THEN 'a buffer nobody sized'::public.exposure_standing
            WHEN a.absorbable > 0 THEN 'a buffer with room in it'::public.exposure_standing
            ELSE                       'every buffer sized and empty'::public.exposure_standing END AS standing
FROM      (
    :compose(layers/remainder.sqlc)
) r
JOIN      (
    :compose(layers/absorption.sqlc)
) a USING (filing, layer)
WHERE r.exposure > 1e-9
